From u8aa9b8cc06fdc99c at groups.google.com  Wed May  1 15:36:56 2013
From: u8aa9b8cc06fdc99c at groups.google.com (Bob Carpenter)
Date: Wed, 01 May 2013 15:36:56 +0000
Subject: Re: [stan-dev] unit-tests failing with compiled model test
Message-ID: <aacI2NdLRq8.6i1ARLxxW5UJ@stan-dev.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <aacI2NdLRq8.-5bD-Thr14cJ@stan-dev.groups.google.com>
References: <aacI2NdLRq8.-5bD-Thr14cJ@stan-dev.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-dev/c/aacI2NdLRq8/m/6i1ARLxxW5UJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

You need to define assign_to_var() for fwd-mode
auto-dif vars.  It basically just does an assignment.
You should only need to define the case where both
the left-hand side type is a fwd-mode auto-dif var
and the right side type is double or int.

We can talk more about this tomorrow.

- Bob

