On Thursday, May 2, 2013 6:56:15 PM UTC-4, Andrew Gelman wrote:
> Hi all (especially Bob).  During the times we've discussed discrete sampling, one possibility we've talked about is to work with latent continuous variables.

I talked about constructions like this in my missing data class. At the moment, it is pretty painful to implement in Stan code because there is no support for passing a vector of lower and upper bounds to the latent parameter, which would be a nice feature even if not facing discrete unknowns.

Ben

