Seems hard to do it fully internally. In any event, it would be easier to play around with this idea if you could pass vectors of lower and upper bounds to the declaration of z. Also, models with latent variables determining a nominal are a further difficulty because there would have to be some way to declare the constraint that one of the latents is bigger than the others for each observation but which one is the biggest varies across observations. There isn't an easy way to do that in Stan currently.

Ben

