Sure, but we don't normally use that state outside of actual sampling because it was decided that the sampler would only transform an input sample and not carry the state of the Markov chain internally (technically the state is stored, but it's always overwritten).  Having adaptation really motivates the other approach, where the constructor you note would be much more natural.

