>
> That's the return for the base case in build_tree(...).
>
> I think something like util.n_tree should be returned, but maybe not?

I don't think so.  This is the base case, so the
answer should be 0 or 1.  The boolean returned by
operator<() will be cast to an int with value 0 or 1.
So the above is equivalent to:

     return (util.log_u < util.H0 - h) ? 1 : 0;

