On 5/7/13 11:48 AM, Michael Betancourt wrote:
> So....I may have been premature.  I found two somewhat serious bugs in the NUTS code -- it's amazing they didn't
> manifest as more serious sampling problems (and frustrating, because I had extensively checked for those kinds of
> problems when first writing up the new code -- I have no idea what happened in between).  It seemed like the errors were
> introducing larger gradients which allowed very small differences in floating point calculations to leak into the
> sampler, accumulate, and eventually become nontrivial.  But even after fixing those problems and verifying that NUTS
> behaves as expected, Mac/Windows are different.  I'm still neck deep in code, hopefully something will turn up.
>
> Incidentally, I can at least explain why the Mac/Windows code seems to "diverge".  The numerical differences eventually
> affect the NUTS criterion, and at a given iteration the tree on one machine reaches a deeper depth than on the other.
>   This misaligns the random number generators and the resulting sequence of samples.
>
>
> On Tue, May 7, 2013 at 4:42 PM, Bob Carpenter <ca...@alias-i.com <mailto:ca...@alias-i.com>> wrote:
