If you do

git checkout v1.3.0
git cherry-pick d88b257a
git cherry-pick f06ed309

and run the test.sh script, there are floating point differences (when cross-compiling) in the 14th or 15th digit after just a few iterations (attached). It seems like the floating point differences are accumulating faster after the refactoring, but I don't know if it should block a release.

