In a way, it's reassuring we had differences before,
so bravo for tracking them down, Ben and Marcus!

It would be nice if the arithmetic were more stable,
but I agree with Ben that it shouldn't necessarily
block a release.

What would convince me we're OK is a set of functional tests that
show similar or better performance in terms of mean and variance of
effective sample sizes per second.

I also second Daniel's vote for some more unit testing
at the sampler level.  I see code's already being checked
in along those lines!  As soon as I crawl out from under
the DARPA proposal, I'll lend a hand.

I also agree with Daniel that it'd be very nice to make
the arithmetic more stable.

Daniel suggested blegging [begging on the blog] for help
from someone who's more familiar with floating point issues.
I'm not too proud to beg, but I'd like to wait until things have
stabilized a bit with more unit tests.

- Bob

