On Tuesday, May 7, 2013 4:45:40 PM UTC-4, Daniel Lee wrote:
> Thanks. I didn't seen any builtin make functions, but we might be able to write one? That's beyond my make skills.
>
> An alternative could be creating a permuted list once. Adding additional things automatically in alphabetical order (using filter-out, etc).

I think the simplest portable approach would be to shuffle the .stan files under src/test/gm/model_specs/compiled/ once on the disk with a sequence of

git mv foo.stan XXX_foo.stan

operations where XXX is some unique identifier. It would probably be fine to choose XXX randomly for each .stan file, but it would be slightly better in principle to choose XXX optimally. Then the question becomes should it be optimized to balance across for 4 or 8 cores and how to keep it optimal when new .stan files are added to that directory. And I don't know how to answer those questions.

Ben

