I guess when the "new" in the following code fails (throw an exception), according to here (http://www.parashift.com/c++-faq-lite/memory-pools.html), the compiler generates some code to delete the pointer that is supposed to point to the object we are trying to create.   And this delete is problematic here.

    inline var log1m(const stan::agrad::var& a) {
      return var(new log1m_vari(a.vi_));
    }

So if I overload the delete operator with a no-op for this class, at least the test can finish.

