On Monday, May 13, 2013 5:59:04 AM UTC-4, Michael Betancourt wrote:
> Can we make this optional?  I don't have R installed on all of my machines and the call to RScript without any existence-checking spits out a ton of errors every time make is called.  Also basically makes a R a dependency of stan, which I'd be uneasy with.

I reverted it again. But I don't think it makes R a dependency of Stan; it only makes R necessary to run test-unit. As it stands now, the requirement to run test-unit in a reasonable amount of time is that the machine has to have at least 10GB of RAM at -O0. And we do almost no testing with higher levels of compiler optimization.

Ben

