Could you remind me when the meetings are and send me info on how to
join them remotely?  I've never been able to figure that one out.

I suspect that people will need push privileges to merge pull
requests.  In particular, any merge which isn't clean I believe has to
be done manually.  While this isn't an issue for any  branch which is
tracking master, if an outside contributor sends a pull request which
requires manual merging, then someone has to do it locally.  (See
https://help.github.com/articles/merging-a-pull-request )  Ideally
whoever submits it would track master, but one-off contributors may
not.  (I suppose they could merge locally and then create a separate
pull request, but that seems tedious.)

Cheers,
Marcus

