cores and 32GB or 64GB of memory.  Or maybe even more.
And a solid-state drive.

> 6) Get Hotfoot set up for testing. This is actually close to happening. However, we have to get to the point where each
> individual test conducted by test-all consumes less than 2GB of RAM because the primary Hotfoot server has a 2GB of RAM
