>     testing on the quirkier cases of Windows or Mac llvm-g++-4.2. To get there, we only have to fix two parser bugs
>     (scary warnings about the precedence of >> vs > when overloaded and the implicit template instantiation errors in
>     ast.hpp)
>
>
> I can avoid the implicit template instantiation errors in ast.hpp just by adding #include <string>. That results in
> test-unit passing (with warnings about the precedence of >> vs > still), although I don't know if that was the best fix.
>
> Ben
