Side note about the kronecker product, one of the motivations for that was a model which (effectively) used the Matrix Normal distribution.  An implementation of that distribution is provided in my pull request with the GP stuff which makes implementing the kronecker product less pressing.  In fact, given that without sparse matrices kronecker products are going to be dog slow, I'd suggest against implementing it unless some one has another use case for it.

Cheers,
Marcus

