On Thu, May 23, 2013 at 3:14 PM, Ben Goodrich <goodri...@gmail.com> wrote:

> On Thursday, May 23, 2013 2:53:22 PM UTC-4, Bob Carpenter wrote:
> > What I'd really like to see is something that looks more like
> > unit tests for the models.  Tests that exercise all of the functions
> > being generated by the model rather than how they run as a whole.
>
> I do think we need a test-grad metatarget that just compiles all the models, runs them with --test-grad, and returns 0 iff lp__ is finite and the AD gradient is close to the numerical gradient. But that is more of a unit test of the libstan and stanc than a test of a particular sample.

+1. Let's work on getting that up sometime soon.

>
> To test a sampler, I think we need something like
>
> -- Generate a random correlation matrix
> -- Maybe scale with random standard deviations to get a covariance matrix
> -- Generate lots of multivariate normal data with mean zero and that covariance matrix
> -- Run a sampler
> -- Verify that posterior is not too far from the population parameters
>
> You could play around with how the population gets generated, but in general, we need a set of tests with known populations to supplement all the toy BUGS models.

That looks great start. So you're thinking of running a single model through multiple samplers? Want to write something more concrete and we can find figure out how to put it into a test?

On Thu, May 23, 2013 at 2:23 PM, Peter Li <li.pe...@gmail.com> wrote:
If so, a different set-up for the framework would be to have separate test files for each sampler. (i.e. for bugs_examples/vol/blocker, we could have blocker_nuts_test.cpp, blocer_unit_metro_test.cpp, etc.). Then, if we do not want to test a certain sampler we just don't include that file. But if we do it this way, I think it would end up compiling the model as many times as we want to test it, which would significantly increase the amount of time it takes to run test-models.

That's now how it works. We would could use the folder structure to generate the correct model dependencies. That is, if the tests are in src/test/models/bugs_examples/vol1/blocker/*_test.cpp, the dependency could be: search for src/models/bugs_examples/vol1/blocker/*.stan, replace *.stan with *$(EXE).

Then each model would be compiled once.

Daniel

