>> I find this code strange:
>>
>>      inline var fmax(const stan::agrad::var& a,
>>                      const double& b) {
>>        return a.vi_->val_ >= b ? a : var(b);
>>      }
>>
>> This seems to be a odd case to arise, but if it does, then the
>> gradient will be carried on if it's greater, otherwise a
>> new var is started, but is this really a wanted behavior? Or is it
>> better always return a new var, even if b is higher?
