On 5/31/13 9:19 AM, Michael Betancourt wrote:
> I think there's some confusion.  The problem is not the speed of copying an Eigen::VectorXd into another Eigen::VectorXd
> verses a std::vector, but rather an Eigen::VectorXd into an Eigen::VectorXd verses a std::vector into a std::vector.
>   The pure copy constructor of the Eigen::VectorXd is definitely ass-slow.

That's why I was suggesting allocating a VectorXd by size,
then copying into its memory.  Now I'm not sure it's legal.

I'm about to go follow up all of the stuff from the Eigen
list yesterday.

